From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:23:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Switch redstone lamps a few per tick, and stagger daylight
 detectors

A lamp gives no signal, so when it switches makes no difference to a circuit;
what it costs is relighting around it. Shady_Hollow's street lamps hang off
daylight detectors, and SurvivalGames' End sets the time to night, so all of
them switched on one tick: 210-280 ms on VPS-B for one room, 0.5-1.7 s with
ten rooms sharing the box.

- athena.yml worlds.<name>.redstoneLampsPerTick (default 4): a lamp is queued
  where vanilla would switch it on, or off once its four-tick delay is up, and
  the world switches that many per tick after its scheduled ticks, checking the
  lamp's power again first. 0 switches at once, as vanilla.
- staggerDaylightDetectors (default true): each detector reads the light on a
  tick of the second chosen from its position, not all on time % 20 == 0.

Shady_Hollow's End on VPS-B: the longest tick 209-279 ms before, 32-48 ms with
the defaults, and every lamp ends as vanilla leaves it
(audit/2026-11-04/lamp-queue/RESULTS.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

